 - **observer**: every state change but `finding record`, `finding resolve` and `ask --kind blocked --finding ID` (in client mode: `finding dismiss`, `note`, other asks, the planning commands, `request add` / `request decline`, `mark`, the dialogue and operations the person and the inbox run (`answer`, `hold`, `recover`, `report`, ...), `agent eval`, `agent cases` and `agent decide` are `authorization_denied`; its reads, `ci failures` (`ci.read`), `agent results` / `agent result` and `agent sets` / `agent set` are answered, the rest `no_use_case`).
 - **executor-telemetry** (no `DAGQ_ROLE`: a queue service principal the control side issues a token of, for one run or one target of no run, to the process that runs an agent, never to the agent): every use case but `telemetry_report`, a read included, and `telemetry_report` of any target but its token's or of a session the control side did not register to that target (`authorization_denied`).
 - **inbox**: nothing a person may do (it acts on the person's word) but `setup-review --yes`; landing and pushing themselves are the integrator's, reached through `integrate`. It registers no work itself: a plan the person asks for goes to a runtime planner as a request (`request add`, `skills/dagq-inbox/reference/requests.md`).
